.TH labctl 1 "January 2026" "linux-labs 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
labctl \- manage Linux labs (setup, grade, cleanup)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B labctl
.I COMMAND
.RI [ LAB_NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B labctl
is a helper tool to run hands-on Linux labs provided by the linux-labs package.
It can prepare a lab environment, grade the final state, and clean up afterwards.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Prepare the environment for the specified lab.
Example: 
.B labctl setup files-01
.TP
.B grade
Run the lab's grading script and print a concise summary of checks.
Example:
.B labctl grade files-01
.TP
.B list
List available labs in a two-column table showing the lab name and a brief one-line description. The description is parsed from the lab's
.I setup.sh
OBJECTIVE section, or falls back to the first header in
.I solution.md
when available.
.TP
.B solution
Display the solution for the specified lab by printing its
.I solution.md
file. Uses
.B less
when available, otherwise prints to standard output.
Example:
.B labctl solution files-01
.TP
.B cleanup
Remove lab-created files and restore the system to its pre-lab state.
Example:
.B labctl cleanup files-01
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
labctl setup users-01
labctl grade users-01
labctl cleanup users-01
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
The grading command exits 0 on success (no failed checks) and 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR firewall-cmd (1),
.BR nmcli (1)
.SH AUTHORS
linux-labs maintainers.
